  "title": "First declension: nouns in -a",
  "note": "Nouns are listed with gender: rosa (f), rose. First-declension nouns end in -a, genitive -ae, and are feminine except words for men's jobs, like nauta (m), sailor. Singular: -a (subject), -ae (of), -ae (to, for), -am (object), -a (by, with). Plural: -ae, -arum, -is, -as, -is.",
